Committed as 3476edb4. If a .yoyo.toml has a quoted value with no closing quote, or a [section header with no ], yoyo now prints a warning on stderr naming each file:line. It prints once per run. Formatting, clippy, the full cargo test run and tests/harness_logic.sh all pass.

What changed
• `src/config_syntax.rs` (new): a checker that finds the two problems, the function that writes the warning, and a print-once switch. The path in the warning is cleaned with sanitize_for_display first. The warning has no special glyphs and uses the same warning: prefix as the #1028 bad-number warning.
• Lines that must not trigger it: a closed value followed by a # comment, an escaped \", one-line arrays, the extra lines of a multi-line array, [mcp_servers.x], and multi-byte text all pass without a warning. Unquoted values (echo it's done) and """ strings are left alone on purpose. The parser accepts both, and calling either an "unterminated quote" would be wrong.
• Values still read exactly as before. The stray quote stays in the value and the exit code stays 0. This change only adds the warning.

Two things the plan didn't expect
• Two extra readers. yoyo config get and config show read the file themselves and never go through load_config_file. After wiring only the loader, the issue's own example (config get model) still printed no warning. So handle_config_get and handle_config_show in src/commands_config.rs (not in the planned file list) each got the same one-line call.
• `config.rs` was already at its size limit. It sat exactly at the 4762-line cap in tests/module_size.rs, so adding even the call would have failed that test. The three identical branches in load_config_file now share one helper, accept_loaded_config, which brought the file down to 4755 lines.

Checks run
• `config get model` on the broken file: prints warning: config file is malformed (1 syntax problem); … .yoyo.toml:2: unterminated quote.
• `-p` with both problems in the file: exactly one warning line in stderr, even though the config file is loaded several times per run.
• A valid file: stdout and stderr from config get model and config show are byte-for-byte the same as the binary before this change.
• Sabotage check: turning off the open-quote check fails only detected_shapes_fire_on_the_right_line. With it restored, everything passes.

I also added a troubleshooting entry in docs/src/troubleshooting/common-issues.md and an entry for the new file in ARCHITECTURE.md.
